WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:04.250
My name is Kellsie Zapata,

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.970
and I am a team member at
Zapata's Cleaning Services.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:11.380
Today, we'll be showing you
how we deep clean a kitchen,

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:15.210
especially the areas
that are commonly missed.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.890
A lot of places that are missed

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.040
are places that are just not seen.

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.648
So, for example,

00:00:20.648 --> 00:00:23.414
you don't see behind your refrigerator,

00:00:23.414 --> 00:00:25.870
you don't see behind your oven,

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.420
you don't see where your hood filter goes.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.610
It's something that's commonly missed.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.650
And if items like these
are not cleaned properly,

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.460
they're not going to last very long

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.226
and you're going to get a lot of dirt,

00:00:37.226 --> 00:00:38.492
debris, and buildup.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.010
Most kitchens will have the filters.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.170
They're always going
to be above the stove.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:50.360
This was a outdoor hood vent filter.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.487
So I think maybe it being outside

00:00:52.487 --> 00:00:55.640
made it much more worse,
because of the weather.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.020
So, once we have our gloves on,

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.430
we take all the pieces down carefully,

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:02.500
and then we spray it down
with our favorite degreaser,

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.500
which is Dawn Powerwash.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:08.130
The worse the buildup,
the more I'll let it soak.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:11.990
So these, we let it soak
for about a good 30 minutes.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:13.115
We turned the hot water on,

00:01:13.115 --> 00:01:14.215
let it run for a few seconds,

00:01:14.215 --> 00:01:15.980
and then we rinsed it all off.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:18.130
One of their jobs is to capture the grease

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:21.230
while you're cooking, and
that grease can build up

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.690
and turn into thick layers of grease.

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:26.680
And that's why you want
to clean them regularly,

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:28.146
at least once a month,

00:01:28.146 --> 00:01:31.004
maybe even more if you cook a lot,

00:01:31.004 --> 00:01:34.100
so that all that grease can get cut down

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:37.223
and the filter can continue
to do its job properly.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.890
We had to get a scrub brush

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.315
to kind of get some of the pieces,

00:01:42.315 --> 00:01:43.390
but for the most part,

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:45.290
the Dawn was able to lift all of that.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.030
This is an older-looking one.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:49.338
They all look differently,

00:01:49.338 --> 00:01:50.830
but they all do the same job.

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:53.590
Their job is to circulate
the air and catch the grease,

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:55.610
which is why you see those brown marks.

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:58.080
That's all grease buildup.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.630
So your filter should not look like that.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:03.610
If it does look like that,
you need to clean it.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:05.190
And it's important to remember

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:08.031
that not cleaning those hood filters

00:02:08.031 --> 00:02:09.656
is also a smoke hazard,

00:02:09.656 --> 00:02:11.180
because that steam and smoke

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.497
is going to stay in that filter.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:17.725
Down here in Georgia,

00:02:17.725 --> 00:02:19.740
we deal with a lot of hard water.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.265
So a lot of that buildup,

00:02:21.265 --> 00:02:23.430
besides the grease that you see,

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:27.270
a lot of those white marks
are just hard-water buildup.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.400
We put our gloves on.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.000
We did not want to
touch anything in there.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.716
And we put our mask on

00:02:32.716 --> 00:02:36.641
because the smell was very foul.

00:02:36.641 --> 00:02:39.090
We pulled out all the filter pieces.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:41.430
We did soak it in hot water and vinegar

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:45.810
to try to loosen as much
of that food debris off.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.418
So, vinegar is acidic,

00:02:48.418 --> 00:02:50.626
so it will eat away at things.

00:02:50.626 --> 00:02:52.890
It's a really good natural cleaner.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:55.680
It worked, but there was
still stuff caked on there.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.350
We went in with the Dawn Powerwash,

00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:58.850
let it sit for about 20 minutes,

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:01.670
and then it looked brand new afterwards.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:03.780
Then we tackled the dishwasher.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.070
I poured vinegar all on the bottom

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:08.580
of the dishwasher to mask the smell.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.040
They were there for six months.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.930
There was food, just
food, pieces of chicken

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:14.900
that were just stuck in the inside of it.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.550
So there's no way that they
were rinsing the dishes.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:21.610
Then, when I realized
how thick the grease was,

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:24.260
we had to bring out our Dupray steamer.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:25.760
And once we brought our steamer out,

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:29.500
it made the cleaning so quick and easy.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.191
The grease was lifting,

00:03:31.191 --> 00:03:33.374
the hard-water marks were lifting.

00:03:33.374 --> 00:03:36.958
The steamer will sanitize, degrease,

00:03:36.958 --> 00:03:39.223
and disinfect, all with water.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:43.750
So, once everything was
clean, to an extent,

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.510
we put all the filter pieces back,

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:47.120
we locked them into place,

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.400
we put the racks back in,

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.750
and then we got an
Affresh dishwashing tablet

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:56.090
and we put it where the
detergent pods go in,

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:00.303
and then we ran a normal, high-heat cycle.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.010
So, with a normal dishwasher,

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.680
first thing we do is we
always take out the filter,

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.840
scrub it with some hot
water and some vinegar

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.420
to get any food debris off,

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.210
rinse it with water,
put it back into place,

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:14.470
and then I'll get some vinegar

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:17.070
and spray the harder-to-reach areas,

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:19.220
like where the sealant part is.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.740
I'll spray that with the vinegar,

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:22.650
scrub it with a grout brush,

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.241
and I'll put everything back

00:04:24.241 --> 00:04:26.241
and I'll use an Affresh tablet.

00:04:26.241 --> 00:04:28.080
Or if I don't have those on me that day,

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.300
I will pour some vinegar
into a dishwasher-safe cup,

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:37.060
put it on the top rack, and
run a hot, normal cycle.

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:39.400
The vinegar will lift any soap scum,

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:43.470
grime, or any other sticky residue.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:46.580
So, after your vinegar
cycle, pull out the rack,

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:48.310
take out that cup of vinegar,

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:49.700
and then we'll pour baking soda

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:52.150
on the bottom of the dishwasher,

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:55.290
close it back up, and run
another hot, normal cycle.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:58.020
And the baking soda will
really help deodorize

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.420
and take out any weird smells in there.

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:03.330
It's important to use these
two products separately.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:04.720
You don't want to use them together,

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:05.745
'cause if you use them together,

00:05:05.745 --> 00:05:07.760
they turn into salt.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:09.426
You want to clean this appliance

00:05:09.426 --> 00:05:10.884
at least once a month.

00:05:10.884 --> 00:05:13.540
This is because a dirty filter

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.873
is not going to get your dishes clean.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.370
You're going to come across lots of dust

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:22.530
and just whatever has
slid under your fridge.

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:25.000
And also, if you have pets,

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.570
there's going to be a lot
of pet hair back there, too.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:30.630
After we safely move the refrigerator,

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.890
you don't want to yank it,
you don't want to pull it

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.670
because it is going to
be connected with a wire.

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:36.940
Just kind of check the area

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.360
and make sure there's no loose wires

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:39.880
before you just start vacuuming.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:43.146
And we start vacuuming the baseboard,

00:05:43.146 --> 00:05:44.929
the wall, the coils

00:05:44.929 --> 00:05:47.273
to get all that dirt and dust off.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.963
We used a foaming action spray.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:54.810
We used a microfiber cloth,

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:58.740
because that's really good
at trapping dust and dirt.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:01.498
You want to at least pull that out

00:06:01.498 --> 00:06:03.220
two to three times a year.

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:04.845
If you have a bigger family

00:06:04.845 --> 00:06:06.120
and you have a lot of pets,

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:08.530
you probably want to do it more,

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:11.073
but at least a minimum
of three times a year.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.050
Cleaning the inside of a oven

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:16.770
is probably the last thing you want to do

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:18.450
after cleaning your whole kitchen.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:21.200
So the more you let the oven go,

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.730
the worse it's going to get.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:26.260
So that's just cooking
oils and food splatter.

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:29.300
So, first thing we do
is pull out the racks,

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.425
and we will spray the racks down

00:06:31.425 --> 00:06:33.375
with the blue Easy-Off.

00:06:33.375 --> 00:06:36.320
And the reason that we use
the blue can of Easy-Off

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:39.144
is because that is an oven cleaner

00:06:39.144 --> 00:06:42.960
that is safe for self-cleaning ovens.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.293
Once we spray the racks,

00:06:45.293 --> 00:06:47.084
we then go back to the oven,

00:06:47.084 --> 00:06:49.710
and we will check out
the bottom of the oven.

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:53.730
And if there's any loose
or burned food debris,

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:55.650
we will wipe all that
out with paper towels,

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:57.700
try to get as much of
that loose food debris

00:06:57.700 --> 00:06:59.620
off the bottom of the oven,

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.050
and then we go in with the Easy-Off

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:04.200
and just spray a generous
amount of product.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:06.650
And then we close the door and let it sit

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.330
a minimum of one hour and 15 minutes

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:11.343
depending on how bad the buildup is.

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:16.700
We go in with SOS pads and
scrub and scrub and scrub

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:18.120
until everything comes off.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:22.730
They are a type of steel
wool abrasive pads,

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:26.730
and they are the thickest
grit that you can use.

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:37.020
We'll wipe that first layer of
product off with paper towels

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:39.270
to get as much of it off as possible.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:42.380
And then the key is to rinse with water.

00:07:42.380 --> 00:07:45.960
So we'll spray water, we'll
wipe, we'll wipe again,

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:47.000
and we'll wipe again.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:50.380
Because one common question
we get with this product

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:53.280
is, "I've used it, but it
leaves a white residue."

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:54.690
Well, that's because you didn't rinse.

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:56.270
You're going to want to rinse your oven

00:07:56.270 --> 00:07:58.497
at least four or five times

00:07:58.497 --> 00:08:01.013
to ensure that all that
product is taken off

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:03.313
and nothing stays behind.

00:08:03.313 --> 00:08:05.610
About once a month,
give it a deep cleaning.

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:08.950
We do not encourage the
self-clean oven cycle.

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:12.483
There is way too many risk
and fire hazards with that.

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:16.550
You know, when you cook on your stove top,

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.860
grease and food's going to splatter,

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:21.130
and it can fall on the sides of the oven.

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:24.540
In this particular instance,
we used a Scour Daddy,

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:26.390
which, a Scour Daddy is really good

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:29.720
at lifting thick grease, caked-on grease.

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:31.610
We used the Sprayway cleaner too

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:33.370
because it has that foaming action

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:36.480
that can really lift all that buildup.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.420
And then we just kind of went back over it

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:40.610
to make sure everything was taken off.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:42.240
Bugs will definitely get drawn in there,

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:45.460
especially if there's food
that gets stuck in there.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:46.830
So when you pull it out,

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.290
you might see some dead
bugs stuck in there.

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:50.380
And if you're ever wondering

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.900
if there's a foul odor in your kitchen,

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:53.983
pull out your oven.

00:08:53.983 --> 00:08:56.558
There might be some stuff
that's gotten behind the oven

00:08:56.558 --> 00:08:58.063
and on the sides of the oven.

